IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wrca-dates`
IMPORT `wrca-core`

-- Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988 (Tas) -- the employer's questions.
--
-- SEAT: the employer of an injured worker, read with its licensed insurer (s 39 lets either give the status notice). The
-- text puts real, dated duties on this party: tell the worker of the right to claim within 14 days (s 33A), notify the
-- insurer within 3 working days and forward the claim within 5 (s 36), give the status of the claim within 28 days (s 39),
-- start weekly payments on the first pay day or within 14 days (s 81), and dispute liability within 84 days or be taken
-- to have accepted it (ss 81A, 81AB); and it creates offences only the employer can commit (ss 33A, 36(3), 39, 81). So
-- it has a seat of its own, beside the worker's in wrca-seat.l4. "Am I liable? What must I do, and by when? Have I met
-- my duties, and is a missed deadline a breach? What must I pay? What is the most I can be fined?" The rules are in
-- wrca-core.l4; this module builds the core's records from plain answers and restates no rule. Its names differ from the
-- worker seat's, so a case file can import both.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act -- the employer's questions`

§§ `Am I liable to compensate this worker?`

@export Am I liable to compensate this worker for this injury under the Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988 (Tas) (s 25, s 3)?
GIVEN `the person works for me under a contract of service or a training contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person works for you as an employee (a contract of service, written or not) or as an apprentice or trainee under a training contract; not as an independent contractor
      `the worker's injury is a disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is a disease (any ailment, disorder, defect or morbid condition), rather than an injury such as a fall, cut or strain
      `the injury arose out of or in the course of the work for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an injury that is not a disease: whether it arose out of, or happened in the course of, the person's work for you
      `the worker was hurt travelling, absent, or at an off-site social or sporting event, without my request or authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury happened while travelling between home and work or between two employers, while temporarily away from the workplace on a working day, or at a social or sporting activity away from work, in each case not at your request or direction or with your authority (s 25(6))
      `the work for me was the major or most significant factor in the disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a disease: whether the employment with you was the major or most significant factor contributing to it
      `the disease is a mental one arising mainly from my reasonable management action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a disease: whether it is an illness or disorder of the mind arising substantially from your reasonable action to transfer, demote, discipline, counsel or dismiss the worker, reasonable administrative action, or a reasonable refusal of a promotion, transfer or benefit
      `the worker's serious and wilful misconduct caused the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is attributable to the worker's own serious and wilful misconduct
      `the injury caused death or serious and permanent incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury resulted in the worker's death or serious and permanent incapacity
      `the worker injured themselves intentionally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was intentionally self-inflicted
GIVETH A `Liability answer`
`Am I liable to compensate this worker` MEANS
    `the employer's liability under s 25`
        (`Liability facts` WITH
            `the person works for the employer under a contract of service or a training contract`                          IS `the person works for me under a contract of service or a training contract`
            `the injury is a disease`                                                                                      IS `the worker's injury is a disease`
            `the injury arose out of or in the course of the employment`                                                   IS `the injury arose out of or in the course of the work for me`
            `the injury occurred in circumstances that s 25(6) says do not arise from the employment`                     IS `the worker was hurt travelling, absent, or at an off-site social or sporting event, without my request or authority`
            `the employment was the major or most significant factor contributing to the disease`                         IS `the work for me was the major or most significant factor in the disease`
            `the disease is an illness or disorder of the mind arising substantially from reasonable management action`  IS `the disease is a mental one arising mainly from my reasonable management action`
            `the injury is attributable to the worker's serious and wilful misconduct`                                    IS `the worker's serious and wilful misconduct caused the injury`
            `the injury resulted in the death or serious and permanent incapacity of the worker`                          IS `the injury caused death or serious and permanent incapacity`
            `the injury was intentionally self-inflicted`                                                                  IS `the worker injured themselves intentionally`)

§§ `What must I do on a claim, and by when?`

@export By when must I tell this worker, in the prescribed form, that they may have a right to claim compensation (s 33A, reg 19, Sch 1)?
GIVEN `the day the worker told me of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker informed you of the injury
      `the worker told me by serving a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were first informed of the injury by the worker's claim for compensation being served on you
GIVETH A `Right-to-claim notice answer`
`By when must I tell this worker of the right to claim` MEANS
    `the s 33A notice` `the day the worker told me of the injury` `the worker told me by serving a claim`

GIVEN week IS A `Working week`, closures IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Workplace days`
`my workplace days` week closures MEANS
    `Workplace days` WITH
        `the normal working week of the place of employment`                                                 IS week
        `closure days in the first week after the claim was received`                                        IS closures

@export By when must I notify my insurer of this worker's claim (s 36(1AA))? Late notice leaves me without indemnity for the weekly payments meanwhile
GIVEN `the day I received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the worker's claim for compensation
      `I have a licensed insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you insure with a licensed insurer (false if you are a self-insurer)
      `the normal working week at the workplace` IS A `Working week` @desc The days on which work is normally carried on at the worker's place of employment
      `days the workplace is closed in the week after the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in the week after receiving the claim fall in that normal working week but the workplace is closed (public holidays, a shutdown)
GIVETH AN `Insurer deadline answer`
`By when must I notify my insurer of this claim` MEANS
    `the s 36(1AA) deadline to notify the insurer` `the day I received the claim` `I have a licensed insurer` (`my workplace days` `the normal working week at the workplace` `days the workplace is closed in the week after the claim`)

@export By when must I forward the completed claim and a copy to my licensed insurer (s 36(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the day I received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the worker's claim for compensation
      `I have a licensed insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you insure with a licensed insurer (false if you are a self-insurer)
      `the normal working week at the workplace` IS A `Working week` @desc The days on which work is normally carried on at the worker's place of employment
      `days the workplace is closed in the week after the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in the week after receiving the claim fall in that normal working week but the workplace is closed (public holidays, a shutdown)
GIVETH AN `Insurer deadline answer`
`By when must I forward the claim to my insurer` MEANS
    `the s 36(1)(b) deadline to forward the claim` `the day I received the claim` `I have a licensed insurer` (`my workplace days` `the normal working week at the workplace` `days the workplace is closed in the week after the claim`)

@export By when must I (or my insurer) notify the worker in writing whether liability is accepted, or why no decision has been made (s 39)?
GIVEN `the day I received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the worker's claim for compensation
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I tell the worker the status of the claim` MEANS
    `the s 39 deadline for the status notice` `the day I received the claim`

@export By when must I start paying this worker's weekly payments (s 81(1))?
GIVEN `the day I received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the worker's claim for compensation
      `the worker's first pay day after that` IS A DATE @desc The first day after receiving the claim on which the worker would normally be paid wages
      `it is reasonably practicable to start on that pay day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If that pay day is within 14 days of the claim: whether it is reasonably practicable for you to start payments on it
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I start weekly payments` MEANS
    `the s 81 deadline to commence weekly payments` `the day I received the claim` `the worker's first pay day after that` `it is reasonably practicable to start on that pay day`

@export From what date must I pay this worker's weekly payments (s 81(3))?
GIVEN `the day the worker's incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker first became unable to work, wholly or partly, because of the injury
      `the day the worker gave me the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker gave you the claim for compensation (with its medical certificate)
GIVETH A DATE
`From what date must I pay weekly payments` MEANS
    `the day weekly payments are payable from under s 81(3)` `the day the worker's incapacity began` `the day the worker gave me the claim`

@export If I dispute liability, by when must I serve the worker written notice with reasons and refer the matter to the Tribunal (s 81A(1))?
GIVEN `the day I received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the worker's claim for compensation
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I dispute liability` MEANS
    `the s 81A deadline to dispute liability` `the day I received the claim`

@export Am I taken to have accepted liability for this claim because I did not dispute it in time (ss 81A, 81AB)?
GIVEN `the day I received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the worker's claim for compensation
      `I have served a dispute notice with reasons and referred it to the Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have done all three: served the worker written notice that you dispute liability, informed the worker of your reasons, and referred the matter to the Tribunal
      `the day I did the last of those` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day you completed the last of the three steps (otherwise any date)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH AN `Acceptance answer`
`Am I taken to have accepted liability for this claim` MEANS
    `whether liability is taken to have been accepted under s 81AB` `the day I received the claim` `I have served a dispute notice with reasons and referred it to the Tribunal` `the day I did the last of those` `today`

§§ `Have I met my duties on this claim? Is a missed deadline a breach?`

DECLARE `My duty statuses` HAS
    `telling the worker of the right to claim (s 33A)`                                                   IS A `Duty status`
    `notifying my insurer (s 36(1AA))`                                                                   IS A `Duty status`
    `forwarding the claim to my insurer (s 36(1)(b))`                                                    IS A `Duty status`
    `notifying the status of the claim (s 39)`                                                           IS A `Duty status`
    `starting weekly payments (s 81)`                                                                    IS A `Duty status`

GIVEN n IS A `Right-to-claim notice answer`, done IS A BOOLEAN, day IS A DATE, today IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Duty status`
`the status of my s 33A duty` n done day today MEANS
    CONSIDER n
    WHEN `no notice is needed: the employer was informed of the injury by the service of a claim (s 33A(2))` THEN `not required`
    WHEN `the employer must inform the worker of the right to claim, in the Schedule 1 form, on or before` last THEN `the status of a duty with last day` last done day today

GIVEN a IS AN `Insurer deadline answer`, done IS A BOOLEAN, day IS A DATE, today IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Duty status`
`the status of my insurer duty` a done day today MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `not applicable: the employer has no licensed insurer` THEN `not required`
    WHEN `on or before` last THEN `the status of a duty with last day` last done day today

@export Have I met my duties on this claim so far? Each is met, still open (with its last day), not required, or missed, and a missed one is a breach of the Act (ss 33A, 36, 39, 81)
GIVEN `the day the worker told me of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker informed you of the injury
      `the worker told me by serving a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were first informed of the injury by the worker's claim being served on you
      `the day I received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the worker's claim for compensation
      `I have a licensed insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you insure with a licensed insurer (false if you are a self-insurer)
      `the normal working week at the workplace` IS A `Working week` @desc The days on which work is normally carried on at the worker's place of employment
      `days the workplace is closed in the week after the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in the week after receiving the claim fall in that normal working week but the workplace is closed
      `the worker's first pay day after the claim` IS A DATE @desc The first day after receiving the claim on which the worker would normally be paid wages
      `it was reasonably practicable to start on that pay day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If that pay day was within 14 days of the claim: whether it was reasonably practicable to start payments on it
      `the claim is for weekly payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for weekly payments for incapacity (not only for expenses)
      `I have told the worker of the right to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the worker the Schedule 1 notice of the right to claim
      `the day I told the worker` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day (otherwise any date)
      `I have notified my insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have notified your insurer of the claim
      `the day I notified my insurer` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day (otherwise any date)
      `I have forwarded the claim to my insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have forwarded the completed claim and a copy to your licensed insurer
      `the day I forwarded the claim` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day (otherwise any date)
      `the worker has been told the status of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your insurer has notified the worker in writing whether liability is accepted, or why no decision has been made
      `the day the worker was told` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day (otherwise any date)
      `I have started weekly payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have started making weekly payments to the worker
      `the day I started them` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day (otherwise any date)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `My duty statuses`
`Have I met my duties on this claim` MEANS
    `My duty statuses` WITH
        `telling the worker of the right to claim (s 33A)`   IS `the status of my s 33A duty` (`the s 33A notice` `the day the worker told me of the injury` `the worker told me by serving a claim`) `I have told the worker of the right to claim` `the day I told the worker` `today`
        `notifying my insurer (s 36(1AA))`                   IS `the status of my insurer duty` (`the s 36(1AA) deadline to notify the insurer` `the day I received the claim` `I have a licensed insurer` `the workplace`) `I have notified my insurer` `the day I notified my insurer` `today`
        `forwarding the claim to my insurer (s 36(1)(b))`    IS `the status of my insurer duty` (`the s 36(1)(b) deadline to forward the claim` `the day I received the claim` `I have a licensed insurer` `the workplace`) `I have forwarded the claim to my insurer` `the day I forwarded the claim` `today`
        `notifying the status of the claim (s 39)`           IS `the status of a duty with last day` (`the s 39 deadline for the status notice` `the day I received the claim`) `the worker has been told the status of the claim` `the day the worker was told` `today`
        `starting weekly payments (s 81)`                    IS `the s 81 status`
    WHERE
        `the workplace` MEANS `my workplace days` `the normal working week at the workplace` `days the workplace is closed in the week after the claim`
        `the s 81 status` MEANS
            IF `the claim is for weekly payments`
            THEN `the status of a duty with last day` (`the s 81 deadline to commence weekly payments` `the day I received the claim` `the worker's first pay day after the claim` `it was reasonably practicable to start on that pay day`) `I have started weekly payments` `the day I started them` `today`
            ELSE `not required`

@export For which days does my insurer not have to indemnify me for weekly payments, because I notified it of the claim late (s 36(4), (5))?
GIVEN `the day I received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the worker's claim for compensation
      `the day I notified my insurer` IS A DATE @desc The day you notified your insurer of the claim
      `I have a licensed insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you insure with a licensed insurer (false if you are a self-insurer)
      `the normal working week at the workplace` IS A `Working week` @desc The days on which work is normally carried on at the worker's place of employment
      `days the workplace is closed in the week after the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in the week after receiving the claim fall in that normal working week but the workplace is closed
GIVETH AN `Indemnity gap answer`
`For which days does my insurer not indemnify me` MEANS
    `the s 36(4) period` `the day I received the claim` `the day I notified my insurer` `I have a licensed insurer` (`my workplace days` `the normal working week at the workplace` `days the workplace is closed in the week after the claim`)

@export What is the most I can be fined for this offence about a claim or weekly payments, in penalty units (ss 33A, 36(3), 39, 81(2))?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Employer offence` @desc The offence: not informing the worker of the right to claim (s 33A(1)); refusing to receive a claim, hindering a claim, or dismissing a worker for claiming (s 36(3)); not notifying the status of the claim (s 39(1)); or not commencing weekly payments as s 81(1) requires (s 81(2))
      `the days the offence has continued` IS A NUMBER @desc For not commencing weekly payments: the number of days the failure has continued (0 otherwise)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined` MEANS
    `the maximum fine in penalty units for` `the offence` `continuing for` `the days the offence has continued`

@export What infringement notice penalty, in penalty units, may I be given for this offence instead of prosecution (reg 28, Sch 2)?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Employer offence` @desc The offence: s 33A(1), s 36(3), s 39(1) or s 81(2), as listed
      `I am a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, the employer, are a company or other body corporate (false for an individual)
GIVETH AN `Infringement answer`
`What infringement notice penalty applies` MEANS
    `the infringement notice penalty for` `the offence` `by a body corporate or not` `I am a body corporate`

§§ `How much must I pay this worker?`

@export What are this worker's normal weekly earnings for workers compensation (ss 69(2), (2A), (14), 70(2))?
GIVEN `the day the worker's continuous employment with me began` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker's continuous employment with you began
      `the day the worker's incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker first became unable to work, wholly or partly, because of the injury
      `all I paid the worker for work in the relevant period` IS A NUMBER @desc Everything you paid the worker for work in the 12 months before the incapacity (or since the start, if less), in dollars, including overtime, bonuses and allowances
      `the overtime part` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that was for overtime or hours beyond the minimum guaranteed contracted hours, in dollars
      `the overtime was required by the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether overtime or excess hours were a requirement of the worker's contract of employment
      `the overtime was regular and rostered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker worked it in a regular and established pattern, in accordance with a roster
      `the overtime was the same number of hours each time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the pattern was substantially uniform in the number of hours
      `the worker would have kept working that overtime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker would have kept working overtime in that pattern if not incapacitated
      `the discretionary bonus part` IS A NUMBER @desc How much you paid at your discretion as a bonus, gratuity or similar payment, in dollars (left out)
      `the allowances part` IS A NUMBER @desc How much you paid to cover special expenses of the job, or as travel, meal or accommodation allowances, in dollars (left out)
      `the worker had more than one employer when the incapacity began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker had contracts of service with two or more employers when the incapacity began
      `the worker's average weekly earnings in other jobs` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: the worker's average weekly earnings in the other jobs, added together, in dollars (0 if none)
      `which of the worker's jobs is full-time` IS A `Full-time contract` @desc If more than one employer: which contract, if any, is full-time (for another employer's, the average weekly earnings in it)
      `another of my workers does comparable work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the worker had worked for you 14 days or less: whether another of your workers does comparable work
      `that other worker's normal weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: that worker's normal weekly earnings, in dollars (otherwise 0)
      `the worker's hourly rate of pay` IS A NUMBER @desc If 14 days or less: the hourly rate under the contract or award, without overtime or shift or other allowances, in dollars
      `the worker's agreed or rostered hours a week` IS A NUMBER @desc If 14 days or less: the hours a week the worker agreed, or was rostered, to work in the pay period of the incapacity
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What are this worker's normal weekly earnings` MEANS
    `the normal weekly earnings`
        (`Earnings facts` WITH
            `the day the incapacity began`                                                                      IS `the day the worker's incapacity began`
            `the day continuous employment with the employer began`                                             IS `the day the worker's continuous employment with me began`
            `everything the employer paid for work in the relevant period`                                      IS `all I paid the worker for work in the relevant period`
            `the part of it paid for overtime or excess hours`                                                  IS `the overtime part`
            `overtime`                                                                                          IS `Overtime facts` WITH
                `the overtime or excess hours were a requirement of the contract of employment`       IS `the overtime was required by the contract`
                `they were worked in a regular and established pattern and in accordance with a roster` IS `the overtime was regular and rostered`
                `the pattern was substantially uniform as to the number of hours`                     IS `the overtime was the same number of hours each time`
                `the worker would have continued to work them in that pattern if not incapacitated`   IS `the worker would have kept working that overtime`
            `the part of it paid at the employer's discretion as a bonus, gratuity or similar payment`          IS `the discretionary bonus part`
            `the part of it paid for special expenses of the employment or as travel, meal or accommodation allowances` IS `the allowances part`
            `the worker had contracts of service with 2 or more employers when the incapacity began`            IS `the worker had more than one employer when the incapacity began`
            `the average weekly earnings in the other employments, added together`                              IS `the worker's average weekly earnings in other jobs`
            `which contract is full-time`                                                                       IS `which of the worker's jobs is full-time`
            `there is another worker of the employer doing comparable work`                                     IS `another of my workers does comparable work`
            `that worker's normal weekly earnings`                                                              IS `that other worker's normal weekly earnings`
            `the hourly rate of pay, without overtime or shift or other allowances`                             IS `the worker's hourly rate of pay`
            `the hours a week the worker agreed or was rostered to work in the pay period of the incapacity`    IS `the worker's agreed or rostered hours a week`)

@export How much must I pay this worker each week before any step-down (s 69(1), (3))?
GIVEN `the worker's normal weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The worker's normal weekly earnings (see "What are this worker's normal weekly earnings"), in dollars
      `the incapacity is certified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the incapacity is supported by a certificate in the approved form signed by a medical practitioner or accredited person
      `the worker is totally incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker is totally incapacitated for work (otherwise partly)
      `the worker's ordinary hourly rate before the incapacity` IS A NUMBER @desc The worker's ordinary-time hourly rate for the work done immediately before the incapacity, in dollars
      `the worker's ordinary hours a week before the incapacity` IS A NUMBER @desc The ordinary hours a week the worker was engaged for immediately before the incapacity
      `the rise in that hourly rate since then` IS A NUMBER @desc How much the ordinary hourly rate for that work has risen (negative if fallen) since the incapacity began, under the contract or award, in dollars
      `what the worker earns or could earn a week in suitable work` IS A NUMBER @desc If partly incapacitated: what the worker is earning, or would be able to earn, a week in suitable employment or business, in dollars (0 if totally incapacitated)
GIVETH A `Weekly payment answer`
`How much must I pay this worker each week before any step-down` MEANS
    `the weekly payment under s 69 for normal weekly earnings of` `the worker's normal weekly earnings`
        (`Incapacity facts` WITH
            `the incapacity is supported by a certificate in the approved form`                                   IS `the incapacity is certified`
            `the incapacity is total`                                                                             IS `the worker is totally incapacitated`
            `the ordinary hourly rate of pay immediately before the incapacity`                                   IS `the worker's ordinary hourly rate before the incapacity`
            `the ordinary hours a week the worker was engaged for immediately before the incapacity`             IS `the worker's ordinary hours a week before the incapacity`
            `the change in the ordinary hourly rate under the contract or industrial instrument since then`       IS `the rise in that hourly rate since then`
            `what the worker is earning or could earn a week in suitable employment or business`                  IS `what the worker earns or could earn a week in suitable work`)

@export Until when must I pay this worker's weekly payments (s 69B(1)(c), (2E), s 87)?
GIVEN `the worker's birth date` IS A DATE @desc The worker's date of birth
      `the worker's pension age` IS A NUMBER @desc The worker's age pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth), in years (67 for anyone born on or after 1 January 1957)
      `the day the worker was injured` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury happened
      `the day the worker was first incapacitated` IS A DATE @desc The date of the worker's initial incapacity from the injury
      `the worker's impairment has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker's permanent impairment has been assessed as a percentage of the whole person
      `the worker's whole person impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc If assessed: the percentage of whole person impairment
GIVETH A `Cessation answer`
`Until when must I pay weekly payments` MEANS
    `the day the entitlement to weekly payments ceases`
        (`Cessation facts` WITH
            `the worker's date of birth`                         IS `the worker's birth date`
            `the worker's pension age in years`                  IS `the worker's pension age`
            `the day of the injury`                              IS `the day the worker was injured`
            `the day of the initial incapacity`                  IS `the day the worker was first incapacitated`
            `the permanent impairment has been assessed`         IS `the worker's impairment has been assessed`
            `the whole person impairment, as a percentage`       IS `the worker's whole person impairment`)
